  "title": "Reasoning controls match each model",
  "summary": "Reasoning requests got more predictable, Claude budget conflicts got explicit errors, and Ideogram found its logo.\n\nText requests now translate `reasoning_effort` into controls each provider accepts. The SDK, MCP schema, and CLI cover all six effort values; legacy thinking fields remain accepted. Claude thinking stays off by default. The generated API docs were also refreshed.\n\nBudget-mode Claude requests keep the requested thinking budget, even when it conflicts with `max_tokens` or `max_completion_tokens`. Bedrock can return a 400 explaining the conflict instead of the proxy silently changing the request.\n\nThe models table now shows the Ideogram brand icon for its v4 turbo, balanced, and quality models.",
